<title>USA: Sierra seeks Columbia/HCA unit.</title>
<headline>Sierra seeks Columbia/HCA unit.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sierra Health Services Inc said Monday it is negotiating to acquire Prime Health Inc and its subsidiary, Med One Health Plan, from a unit of Columbia/HCA Healthcare Corp and two of its partners.</p>
<p>The deal, which is subject to a definitive agreement, due diligence, and regulatory approvals, could close within 90 days.  Terms of the possible deal were undisclosed.</p>
<p>Med One Health Plan operates health maintenance and preferred provider organizations throughout Las Vegas, serving approximately 11,000 HMO members and 140,000 people through administrative services contracts for self-insured employers.</p>
</text>
